    "body": "`parse_dependencies()` did not record `pkg.submodule` for `from pkg cimport submodule`, so `cythonize` did not notice changes to `pkg/submodule.pxd`. It also recorded wrong names: `from pkg cimport sub` followed by an indented `pass` gave `pkg.pass`, a parenthesised list with comments lost every name, and `from . cimport x` gave `..x`, the parent package.\r\n\r\nThe regex for the names after `cimport` was added in #2691 (2018). A fixup in that PR replaced the slice `source[m.end():]` with `pos=m.end()`, where `^` does not match at the start position, so the single-line form never worked in a release. I now use `match()` at that position, accept newlines and comments inside parentheses, skip empty items and `as` aliases, and keep the leading dots of a relative `from`. `from pkg cimport b` followed by an indented `()` no longer raises an `AttributeError`.\r\n\r\nSix of the eight new tests in `TestDependencies.py` fail on master. The other two guard empty parentheses and a long run of spaces.\r\n\r\nI opened this earlier as #8095 and closed it so the issue author could take it. There has been no PR for #8091 in the week since, so I am sending it again here, rebased on current master.\r\n\r\nFixes #8091\r\n",
    "closed_at": null,
